   "description": "Campaigns, channels, audiences and results, so you remember what worked and why.",
   "instructions": "You are building the memory of a marketing team: what was tried, for whom, on which channel, and what happened.\n\n## What to capture\n- **Campaigns** with their dates and goal.\n- **Channels**: Meta, Google Search, TikTok, email, events and so on.\n- **Audiences**: who a campaign was for.\n- **Results**: numbers with their metric and period, exactly as written (CPA €21 in October, not \"good results\").\n- **Creatives**: named ads, videos, landing pages.\n- **Learnings**: what the team concluded, in one sentence each.\n- **Decisions**: budget moves, pauses, launches.\n\n## Links worth making\nran_on, targeted, produced, learned_from, funded, replaced, caused, part_of\n\n## Leave out\nRaw tables with no conclusion, tracking codes, and platform marketing emails."
